<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Riau Archipelago</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Riau Islands</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riau">Riau</a> Archipelago is a group of islands south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a>, including Batam, Bintan and the Lingga islands, now part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>'s Riau Islands province. From the 16th century they were part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a> sultanate, and Bintan became a seat of its court and a centre of Malay culture. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-dutch-treaty-of-1824">Anglo-Dutch Treaty of 1824</a> placed them in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> sphere.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/riau-archipelago.jpg" alt="Riau Archipelago" width="300" height="198" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Doseiai2 at en.wikipedia · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Locator_archriau.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
